# visualizevelocity

- Label: Visualize Velocity
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 80 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/visualizevelocity.html
- Summary (EN): Turns a 2D velocity field into an RGBA layer with the visualization baked in, for debugging or final output. Output: result.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme un champ de vélocité 2D en image RGBA visible, en mode HSV, en traînées (streak) ou en flèches (quiver plot).

- Inputs meaning: ["source: a UV layer providing 2D velocity values"]

- Key parameters: ["Method: HSV (velocity length sets value, direction sets hue; Scale controls magnitude-to-value mapping)", "Method: Streak (particles traced through the flow; Density, Scale, Brightness, Gamma, Seed, Visualize Speed, Speed Min/Max, Ramp, Maximum Steps)", "Method: Quiver Plot (arrows on a grid oriented to velocity; Tile Size, Tile Padding, Shaft Thickness, Head Thickness, Head Ratio, Scale Arrows with Speed, Visualize Speed, Speed Min/Max, Visualization Ramp)", "Speed Min/Max (Streak and Quiver Plot): speed range mapped to the colour ramp or arrow scaling; the Compute Range button fills it from the source length"]

- Caveats: ["Maximum Steps caps streak steps, preventing excessive computation in very fast flows", "The page describes no other limitations"]

